# --- Third-party reference documents, never committed -------------------------
# Publisher manuscript templates are downloadable but not licensed for
# redistribution (docs/adr/0004-docx-renderer.md). They are useful locally as
# reference documents and as conversion targets; committing one would put an
# unrecorded licence assumption into an Apache-2.0 distribution.
# Put any such file here. docs/TEMPLATES.md records where to obtain them.
fixtures/local/

# --- Golden corpus discipline --------------------------------------------------
# Everything under fixtures/ EXCEPT local/ is committed and must carry a licence
# entry in fixtures/LICENSES.md (docs/CORPUS.md rule 1). Large generated
# artifacts are produced by script instead of committed.
fixtures/generated/
fixtures/**/*.tmp

# --- Build output --------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
# scripts/check-surface-parity.mjs writes each surface's conversion here and removes
# the directory in a `finally`. A `finally` does not run when the process is killed —
# a cancelled CI job, a Ctrl-C — and what it leaves behind is eight DOCX files in the
# repository root with no row in fixtures/LICENSES.md. check-docs.mjs catches that,
# correctly and loudly; ignoring the directory means the crash cannot stage them in the
# first place, which is the cheaper half of the same guarantee.
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.next/
.vercel/
# Produced by apps/web/scripts/prepare-assets.mjs: the two browser bundles (built by the
# same functions scripts/check-surface-parity.mjs runs, so the page cannot be running a
# different build from the one the parity gate measured), the Typst WASM, the shipped font
# set, and the demo documents copied out of fixtures/. All generated at build time, because
# a second committed copy is a second thing that can drift — and because check-docs.mjs
# correctly fails an unignored .docx or .pdf anywhere in the tree.
apps/web/public/markforge/

# --- Dependencies --------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# --- Tooling caches ------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.vitest/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.eslintcache

# --- MarkForge runtime state ---------------------------------------------------
# The LLM cache is committable by design when reproducibility is wanted
# (docs/SPEC.md 6.3), so it is NOT ignored here. Probe results are per-deployment
# and machine-specific, so they are.
# .markforge/llm-capabilities.json is deliberately NOT ignored. The committed LLM
# cache records mode:"guided" and a seed, so its entries are only reachable by a
# session that computes the cache key the same way — which needs this record. It
# describes one deployment's capabilities and contains no credential.

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials come from the environment only; no key ever belongs in the repo
# (docs/adr/0009-llm-openai-compatible-only.md).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Editor and OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Office lock files --------------------------------------------------------
# Word and Excel write these next to a file that is open; they are valid ZIP
# containers, so a fixture glob will otherwise try to parse them.
~$*

# Starter table from scripts/diff-mammoth.mjs; triage lives in docs/MAMMOTH-DIFF.md
docs/.mammoth-diff.generated.md
